## Review-comment regression coverage

- MQTT receipt enters a nonblocking FIFO scheduler before handler tasks spawn.
- All 14 registered device-command route shapes resolve raw ids, topic-safe ids,
  names, computed names, and IP aliases to one canonical per-device lane.
- Invalid ids and global/custom discovery status topics do not retain device
  workers; separate devices remain concurrent.
- A synthetic handler panic is isolated and the next same-device command runs.
  The focused test intentionally invokes Rust's panic hook while still passing.
- Sensitivity followed by a Music effect reaches the loopback Platform capture
  server with the new sensitivity in the effect payload.
- Sensitivity notification and slider echoes use a per-device publication lock,
  re-read canonical state after lock acquisition, and publish the newest value
  last under a controlled stale-notify interleaving.
- The read-after-lock guard passed 100/100 repetitions and failed when locally
  mutated to snapshot state before acquiring the publication lock.
- The slider stores under the device-control permit, then schedules its echo in
  the background so MQTT broker I/O blocks neither the permit nor dispatch lane.
- Detached echo failures are explicitly logged; synchronous entity-notification
  publish failures continue to propagate to their caller.

## Existing regression and wire coverage

- Discovery publishes the 0..100 slider only for usable numeric musicMode
  metadata; case variants and malformed/empty metadata remain covered.
- Decimal values round, out-of-range values clamp, and NaN, infinity, overflow,
  and non-numeric MQTT payloads fail explicitly.
- Discovery and state echo share one topic constructor; exact topics, payloads,
  reset behavior, and synchronous publish-error propagation are asserted.
- Platform sensitivity, historical defaults, clamping, autoColor, and packed RGB
  are asserted through payload builders and an in-process HTTP capture server.
- A Music effect plus rgb_color disables autoColor on the wire; ordinary scenes
  in the same command continue to ignore RGB.
- Scene dispatch reads fresh canonical sensitivity and retains the detached-device
  fallback without cloning full device/catalog state.

